  "notes": "{通|とお}す is a versatile transitive verb with three main meanings: letting something pass through, persisting to completion, and showing someone in.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {通|とお}る (intransitive, to pass through)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {光|ひかり}を{通|とお}す: to let light through\n- {針|はり}に{糸|いと}を{通|とお}す: to thread a needle\n- {意見|いけん}を{通|とお}す: to get one's opinion accepted\n- {筋|すじ}を{通|とお}す: to be consistent\n- お{客|きゃく}さんを{通|とお}す: to show a guest in\n\nAS SUFFIX (-{通|とお}す):\nAttaches to verb stems to mean 'do through to completion':\n- {読|よ}み{通|とお}す: to read through entirely\n- やり{通|とお}す: to see through to the end",
